Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["\<\
Kalman Filtering vs. ARMA Models for Stock Trend Extraction and Future Price \
Prediction\
\>", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"c76420c3-e98d-44fc-9944-c97be13deb40"],

Cell["\<\
A Rigorous Comparative Framework in Wolfram Language: Trend Derivation, \
Out-of-Sample Forecasting, and Rolling Walk-Forward Backtesting. \
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"8e09df34-1029-4c4b-91f5-1e766220813c"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["1. Executive Summary and Theoretical Framework", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"9e7a313f-2315-4694-8d10-9e3b7500f0a6"],

Cell["\<\
Predicting future stock prices and extracting dynamic trends are two \
foundational problems in quantitative finance. Two distinct mathematical \
paradigms are commonly employed:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"da8c0ab2-acee-4292-8122-e559b0c22086"],

Cell["\<\
1. Autoregressive Moving Average (ARMA) Models: Rooted in classical \
econometric time series analysis (Box-Jenkins methodology), ARMA models \
capture stationary autocorrelation structures in returns and project them \
forward toward the unconditional long-term drift rate.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"8ddba88d-27f3-4d4f-b4cd-ed01c0503ea0"],

Cell["\<\
2. Kalman Filtering and State-Space Models: Rooted in control theory and \
Bayesian dynamic linear models, Kalman filters estimate unobserved hidden \
states (the true trend level and instantaneous momentum/drift) from noisy \
sequential observations, updating estimates recursively with optimal Bayesian \
variance reduction. \
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4f96087f-0f1c-4da2-82a3-dfb2172e19f1"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Research Objective", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"fcfef0a4-5771-4597-875b-46b4beb659ce"],

Cell["\<\
How accurately can ARMA models and Kalman Filter trend models predict the \
expected future price of a stock (specifically, the expected average price \
over an investment horizon, such as a 20-day trading month)? \
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"70a3cc8d-b259-445e-90a3-f2f03f62e84e"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Mathematical Specification", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"274895a1-34e1-4d59-b482-46e6573ddd61"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["(A) The ARMA Process on Stock Returns", "Subsubsection",ExpressionUUID->"7bf99aaf-9d35-403a-8a59-1d034e09ba6b"],

Cell["\<\
Stock price levels P_t are non-stationary I(1) processes. Direct ARMA \
estimation on raw prices often fails or yields explosive roots (|phi| >= 1). \
We therefore model stationary continuously compounded log returns:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"9866d6a4-8dc2-41fa-9526-124f7fb3570e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "  r",
 StyleBox["t = ln(P",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 "t / P",
 StyleBox["{t-1}) = ln(P",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 "t) - ln(P_{t-1})"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"fb86a523-b029-41ce-9900-b4ff17c19840"],

Cell["An ARMA(p, q) process for returns is defined as:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"23b9193e-c564-4bc9-9d3f-1b75f173609c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "  r",
 StyleBox["t = c + Sum[phi",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 "i  r",
 StyleBox["{t-i}, {i, 1, p}] + eps",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 "t + Sum[theta_j  eps_{t-j}, {j, 1, q}]"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5021fb71-894e-4f95-b486-2fc620e313e1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Given multi-step forecasted returns {r",
 StyleBox["{T+1}, ..., r",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 "{T+H}}, the reconstructed future price trajectory is:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"64869dd9-e780-4188-a532-4c28ebf1fba8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "  P",
 StyleBox["{T+h} = P",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 "T * Exp[Accumulate[{r",
 StyleBox["{T+1}, ..., r",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 "{T+h}}]]"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a642f4a7-202d-4cce-b672-4299d5e8fdfb"],

Cell["The expected average future price over horizon H is:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6c862933-a7fe-49da-8a82-839404f5ed9d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "  P",
 StyleBox["avg",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 "ARMA = (1/H) * Sum[P_{T+h}, {h, 1, H}] "
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b59385c6-85d8-474c-96e8-a5d550ee4286"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["(B) The Local Linear Trend (LLT) Kalman Filter", "Subsubsection",ExpressionUUID->"fa7a1427-a750-49b8-bd88-9704cfe0dda2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The state-space model decomposes price y",
 StyleBox["t = P",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 "t into an unobserved dynamic level mu",
 StyleBox["t and velocity/slope beta",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 "t:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0cfa1f43-dcf2-4f09-a966-0f3a8257c387"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "  Observation Equation:  y",
 StyleBox["t = mu",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 "t + eps",
 StyleBox["t,        eps",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 "t ~ N(0, sigma_eps^2)"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"43e70d03-cd16-44c2-878e-1665d6cb9028"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "  Level Transition:      mu",
 StyleBox["{t+1} = mu",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 "t + beta",
 StyleBox["t + eta",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 "mu",
 StyleBox["t,  eta",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 "mu",
 StyleBox["t ~ N(0, sigma",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 "mu^2)"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0f4b62b6-06fa-42e1-9c53-60e84cbd11cc"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "  Slope Transition:      beta",
 StyleBox["{t+1} = beta",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 "t + eta",
 StyleBox["beta",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 "t,     eta",
 StyleBox["beta",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 "t ~ N(0, sigma_beta^2)"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2254f5bd-c813-4728-8e69-f15090324c25"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Forward extrapolation h steps ahead from terminal state (mu",
 StyleBox["T, beta",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 "T):"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6bc495ff-2b09-49d9-bc8a-a82df69e7356"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "  P",
 StyleBox["{Kalman, T+h} = mu",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 "T + h * beta_T"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"9d5e2a58-55a2-4a10-888c-79b9b509aae7"],

Cell["\<\
The expected average future price over horizon H is analytically:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d3e7ff5b-f260-43cc-98ac-382bef700fd5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "  P",
 StyleBox["avg",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 "Kalman = (1/H) ",
 StyleBox[" Sum[mu_T + h ",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " beta",
 StyleBox["T, {h, 1, H}] = mu",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 "T + ((H + 1) / 2) * beta_T "
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a8350c6c-1cfa-4fa0-b75c-6e8bb549d011"],

